  ⚠ **'Cannot re-derive' is not 'wrong'** — those conclusions may well be correct. They are simply no longer falsifiable by re-running, which is the one thing this project has relied on from round one.

**What this round structurally cannot do**: (1) it ranks re-derivability, never truth; (2) **the instrument cannot be changed** — this corpus exists only in this repository, so cross-instrument replication is structurally unavailable and would require a second machine holding a second copy; (3) a PERMANENT verdict is about **this machine at this moment**; (4) elapsed under parallel load is not a runtime profile — the cap curve bounds slowness from one side only.

